A||N||2||fierose||VSS Cutting  Out?||||4||
Z||000000||fierose||11-02-2001||05:42 PM||||I've had this problem lately with my  speedometer cutting out at about 2000-2500 rpm's.  If I'm in gear and the speedo stops working if I push in on the clutch to let the rpms go down the speedemoter will jump to where it should be.  I went to check it out originally and the hold down bolt was loose.  I took everything out cleaned it and put it back in but still the same problem.  the gear  was in good shape and didn't see any visual problems.  Does this mean my  sensor is toast?  If it is does anyone  know where you can buy one?<P>thanks in advance<BR>85 4cy 5sp.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-02-2001||05:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierose:<BR><B>I've had this problem lately with my  speedometer cutting out at about 2000-2500 rpm's.  If I'm in gear and the speedo stops working if I push in on the clutch to let the rpms go down the speedemoter will jump to where it should be.  I went to check it out originally and the hold down bolt was loose.  I took everything out cleaned it and put it back in but still the same problem.  the gear  was in good shape and didn't see any visual problems.  Does this mean my  sensor is toast?  If it is does anyone  know where you can buy one?<P>thanks in advance<BR>85 4cy 5sp.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Fierose!<BR>Pull it and check the gears a little closer...<BR>I had the same problem, replaced the VSS, no difference...<BR>Changed the gears, and it worked...<BR>I had a SLIGHT cup worn into the sensor gear that would not mate with the tranny gear...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierose||11-03-2001||02:41 PM||||Hey thanks fierowrecker.  I never thought to replace the gear before the VSS.  I can't believe the price on  those thingss.  Does anyone know where you can get those gears though?  Autozone?||||reg||1
